  "term": "kava",
  "definition": "Kava is a substance made from the dried roots and rhizome of Piper methysticum, a plant from Oceania, and is known for calming and sedative effects. The name also refers to a pungent drink prepared from the plant’s roots, and heavy use can cause adverse effects.",
